# Python security

`README.md` wins if this rule disagrees with it. Repo hard lines are in `common-security.mdc`.

- Bind query values with SQLAlchemy parameters. User input stays in arguments. Do not format untrusted input into SQL text. Orphan deletes in `cleanup_service` use a fixed table list; do not append request data to that list.
- Keep thumbnail, frame, and video paths inside their data directories. `resolve_thumbnail_fs_path` refuses a path outside the thumbnail directory. Keep that refusal.
- Do not log decrypted passwords, RTSP URLs that contain credentials, provider keys, HomeKit PINs, or Fernet tokens. When a log must mention a secret, use `mask_sensitive`.
- Outbound HTTP keeps a timeout. Do not disable TLS verification on a new client. `verify_ssl` is an existing per-controller Protect setting; do not make insecure the default for other clients.
- Webhook SSRF checks live in `backend/app/services/webhook_service.py`. Do not weaken them or add a bypass.
- Start a subprocess with an argument list. Do not build a shell string from user input.
- Encrypt secrets with the existing Fernet helpers in `backend/app/utils/encryption.py`. Do not add a second crypto scheme. Do not read or write `ENCRYPTION_KEY` from request data.
